  "notes": [
    "Headings are transcribed from the tables of contents of M4Q(R1) (Module 3) and section 4.2 of M4S(R2) (Module 4), read directly. See docs/regulatory-sources.md.",
    "M4S(R2) states of Module 4: 'This guideline is not intended to indicate what studies are required. It merely indicates an appropriate format for the nonclinical data that have been acquired.' A section absent from a draft is therefore never reported as a deficiency.",
    "An IND is thinner than the marketing application M4Q/M4S describe. FDA's content requirement is 21 CFR 312.23, and this tree is only the organising format.",
    "'requires' lists the kinds of submitted evidence a section is drafted from. It is this service's own mapping, not a regulatory statement about what the section must contain."
  ],
